        <p>As promised last week I herewith publish on inter- esting ptragraph. I find that the author of it ran Nay. Now b.dies ! Surely thiA is an incentive to Irving you rut in any future competition. Let me just say II word to Ilise 11. Carter, who writes the parag.aph. The advice you give is vary good, but it gives too many tints. If sou had taken one part of your psragraph it would have beer) bettrr. But let roe say further, I hope that it will be the means of helping some who need your good advice, especially the points on regulatiry in feeding a most important point to observe.</p>
