        <p>The Warrington I aitclion of the Church Lads' Brigade engaged in Rome intereetiog memeuvres in the neighbourhood of Norton and Halton on hurter Monday. A filen of campaign Lad been drawn up on approved military lines, and, favoured with tine hut not ' too rearm weather, the operations sore carried out in enrert and entirely eatiefactoryle. Cliptain Ford and ' the member. of the Stockton fleathCompany represented the Blue(or Chershire,force who COOlflopleved a surprise attach on Liverpool via the Runcorn Tremports r tiddge and the Warrington companicsAnder Coptoin Ilenehall, comprising the Bed (Lencashire) fut., were told off to frontrate any latflllpt to cross the river. Lit tit...ant- Colonel Appleton octet rot Ode( empire while Mejor Brooke umpired for Blue and tie Adjutant iCeptain Senlie3) for the 11, d. During the mor .ing there sore encounters between the rival farces at Dareshury, the Bede beiog held up for a considerable lime but eventually succeeding in prereing Blue lAck in splendid style. Blue were drier. back in confusion, and they were only saved from complete annihilation by the Blue Impair.° sent out from Norton Perk to cover their retit ems.. Operations were then suspended on loth vi (lea until 230 p.m. The notation formed up and lifter a short oat marched to Halton Common, uhere they proceeded to cook dinners in their owe clnteeur, kinoly provides for each Iva by 1101110 gentlemen of Warririgron nod neighbourhood. The lure were soon frying nt.og., cooking motto° 011 ye, poaching es t s, fey iug ham mcfcc., like net-rue euldime, each lad having brought his yen dinner from home. A load of firewood had been sent very kindly by Mr. Eva. (Fir Richard Brooke's agent) to the hividne. At 230 p.m. frollloollo nnre resumed. Captein Ilenehall oho had now taboo chnitnand of the whole battalion, received owes that the Rltre rearguard wan holding lislton Castle end 110 watt iltttrUCted to</p>
