        <p>'Oran. and attack thev, endelvottr to destroy thero end prevent the canning or the blarney. Ily kind penniesion of Lieutenant-Colonel Fair°lough :4th Smith Lomeashire Regiment), Sergeant Live, of the eyclinte, brought not about half a &amp;teen cyclists . with a plent Hot supply of blank [lll36lllllilinol and rep•e- sented the Cheshire Farce at Helton Castle. Sergeant Lone marked each of the different pt,Piliollll I.e ark up by semaphore flags. Captain Nonfatall now edvecced and the lads extended fairly well, covered no scouts: who were told that they would find the fl Igs tuntking the enerny'e pmetico, but no one hal had any idea that the enemy would Ira real one and that they would It received by • very hot rifle fire. The scoots did not serve Captin Newhall very too 11, sad es far ea the Chief Umpire eaw,no infern.ation wes sent beck to Lim, though the xamaphoring wee very good in the rear of the scouts. The ground tots very much expoeed, lett letter advantage could have been taken Of attit cover there wee, end 11.0 lade did not lie II it down alten)e when haltedwe they eltoul&amp; have dtwe. Sergeant Lowe fell back on Ilalt on Cistle, and Captein Hen, hall gradually advanced op to the loner slopes ef the Ceetle Rock, where he delta( red the final ambit up to the Castle with bugle, ',lowing, &amp;a. Cerise fire colluded at 5.311 p.m., nod fiends nod foe. spin went into bivouac ou flatten Common atd</p>
        <p>Both Stockton Beath en .% St. Paul's Rorie Bind playol at frequect inrerval• and the say in which the lads wing and whistled in the march borne, beaides playing • vigorous gsme of to 46,11 after ten. sprein volumra f..r their phys].pin and for the lanat of the baining they receive. , On cmi cci nt Stag Bridge, Stockton ninth and Christ Church Componire left the liattelion, the renn•inder ronrching to the Drill Doll where they wete disminsed. The tots dome en of St. Beta's Company ported.s rery fine buck skin—which hal hien kindly preaented to the Batts lien by Copt•in W. Beat (late Captain in ilie Royal W.bh Fusilier.) of Vivid, Llangollen. Another akin will thertly he provided for the Lase drum., of Stockton Heath Company Bugle Beni. The Battalion looked smnrt in their new marching order Lit, which consists of their ordinary clothes, CL. B. I pair meet, I hoe pntliea with carbines and the new mess oinlesos in white di ill covers strapped behind the wniattelr, to which it is hoped no ntually to ndd a nockintosh cope for each lad, Ilium making him proof egninet had e nether. The thanks of the Rotation are doe to Sir Richard Brooke. Boot., for permisaion to te e him perk for the marrevres,Rml also to his egent (Mr. Evans) for the pains he took to help the ISattali, n in every way ; oleo to Sergeant LOw• end the cyclists of the 4,11 Battalion South Lencaabire, for their great assistance during the nuoreuvrea.</p>
