        <p>PAINS AFTER EATING-</p>
        <p>HEADACHES</p>
        <p>When your head is dull and heavy, your tongue furred, your bowels costive, and you rise ia the morning tired, with no relish for breakfast and dreading your work ; when you are racked with pains—in the head, chest, back. stomach_all over ; when you are bilious and unable to look at food ; when you feel " doae up," have no appetite, no energy, no interest or ambition—your stomicit and lio:r are out of order. As a result, the decayed products of undigested food are poisoning your blood and sapping your vitality. It may be the weather, or overwork, errors in diet, or constitutional weakness ; but, whatever the cause, your stomach and liver need help, and need it sorely. Mother Seigel's Syrup, made from roots, barks and leaves, provides all the help they need. It will tone up your stomach, renew your appetite, make food nourish you, purify your blood, stimulate your liver to healthy activity, regulate your bowels, and give you new streugai, II2W energy, new life.</p>
