        <p>The vloe,presidents* main at the Liberal Club on F,aster filonday U.ll distinctly popular, and consequently very enjoyable. Beside. a large nrimber of entries, a fair crowd gathered to watch the progree• of the games. which numbered nearly 60. Prenctuality wan a great feature. sod groat prairie is due to Mr. F. Walker, eecretary of the green, for the manner in which the arrangements were carried out. The green was in excellent condition, thanks to the efforts of Mr. Randall, toe club manager. There was some floe bowling, especially when one considers the fact that it was the first game of tie season. The following is a list of the prize winners ;-I,Coun- cillor J Wilkinson,marble cluck; 2, T O'Brien, value of LI se. ; 3, A klynekyrno, value 10s.; 4, J Graham, pair of boots : 5, J Smith, eafety razor ; 6, A Gilbert, vale. 5,.; 11l Forster, value 5..; 0, R Fogg, smoker'. companion. The following is a list of the d3nord of the prices Councillor Wilkinson, Captain Crosfleld, Sir T Locker, Corm, More Halliwell and J T Locker, Alderman Tinnion sod Mr J E Warren. We enderatand that as C .uncillor Wilkinson won his own prize he hes generously offered it to Mr. O'Brien, silo came second. The prize digttibution will take place in Ike immediate future, at a emoking concert at the Liberal Club, when Mr. A. ii. 'roefield is expected to be present.</p>
