        <p>I •cal committee worked loyally with the Mayor as preen'. n', Mr. E. Bratlabaw as honorary treactrer, Mr. Ette4 Morrie an honorary nocretsry. At tie end of last year, with a I ire. to economy and to prevent any pornielv over.lapping in the Rupeel for fund, it wee decided that the Lifsellaat Saturday Fund ahould Fe merg• 4.1 into the ordinary work of the inntitution, ant hence, the lo al committee will, in future, become the Wariangton branch of the inetitotion. Throughout the country, the wisdom of the step tette° by the Com- mittee of !Management has been approved, and those craven workersof the cause in thin locslity, confidently hope thee the same generous sympathy, which waa extended to them as the hifrolloat Setordey Committee will be corn ironed tinder the altered cirattnistancee.</p>
