        <head>Gilbert-.. Ward,</head>
        <p>Gilbert-.. Ward,</p>
        <p>A pr ity wedding ens tobffinisel at Golhorna- -011,1. It 044 Glatreh on Saturday let, e 1,e,) Mies Ada Gitbert, only daughter of Mr and Mrs. El Ward Gi heir, 331. Lovelv-Inne, Warring- ,nn, was mini foul to MI. lie rge Edward Ward, eon of M. George Ward, of Hood- lane, Sankey. The Her. Arthur Urn, of Little Leigh, officiated and the congrega,ion joined in the tirging of the hymn "floppy the home ahem line reigns there." The bride who was given earty by her father wan ratite,' in a tasteful biscuit coloured silk dress, hand e.nbroidered and trimmed with satin. She wore a fine chip hat with cut</p>
        <p>_ African feather to match. Her booths-one bouquet et:resisted of orchids, arum Mire, lilies of the valley, and sprays ofstni'ax. The bridesmaid. were Misses Clara Mabel Trait, (Fnlly-lane) and Annie Mould (of Chorley). They wrote dreaven of pale blue silk voile with silver trimmings end pile blue fringe. Their black lace lids contrasted very nicely. They carried hoiejnete of daffodils with sprays of smilax and fern, Mr. Fred Ward (brother of the bridegroom) discharged the duties r f best men. The reception was held in Oreening's Dining Hal and was attended by about 50 gueds. A large soother of p-meats were received.</p>
        <p>Hawthorn—Sharp. The martiage was solemnized at Mothers Hotel, Dundee, on Saturday, of Councillor Joaeph Hawthorn, eldest ton of the late Mr. Thomas Hawthorn. of Warrington, and Miss Intl-a Foreman Sharp,yountter daughter of Mr. Andrew Sh trp, jute spinner, Alhany-lerrace, Dundee. Tne Mee, W. Nelson officiated.</p>
