        <p>INTERESTING TEST CASE AT FROH.S.FIANI. The magistrate. at the Frodeham Petty Sessions on Wednesday had a iiifilcult point to decide in regard in two itteresting motor caner by the police. Herbert Windase, of 40, hatherine.etreet, Chester, and John Doran, of 43. Wynnetay.atreet, Liverpool, were sum- moned fur having driven motor cern without a light shining on the identification plate et the rear. From the evidence it appeared that Wind/wig TOPS in el arpe of a taxi-crib which had ler n ordered from Chester to tow the car driven by Dorm, which had broken down at Pre.. Brook. The cars were cr rented by a rope eight yards lone, and the hood lights on the second car were lighted to illuminate the rear plate of the first CRT. The defence in the first case was that the car yrra towing a vehicle in the form of a Halter snd the light ehould bare been at the rear of the second cnr according to the Motor.car Act. 'lbis case ens diendseed on payment of costa. lathe sect ad case the defending solicitor maintained that the second i.e ceased to lea motor-ca tinder the meaning of the Act circa it had broken dime, becalme It ceased to be props lied by mechanical poster, .d the driver Wan simply steering a trailer. This cote wee ale, dismissed on puymant of costs. At the same court Jonnthan Carter, of Upper Henk- el reet, War tington, loan ale, ordered to pay the coals for not hnoing the rear plate of bla motor-cycle</p>
