        <p>The statement of accounts for St. James' ahowird art income Horn the general offertory of £lOB Its Rd and from special collections of £74 lOs 41. The total expenditure amounted to £193 16r 41 and there was a balance doe to the bank of LI 10x 91. The total income showed an increase of about £9 on last year. The Whore sheet for St. Hildi's %Melon showed an income of £44 Is 91 and a balance to haud of Li On IIL The accounts were adopted. ST. ANN'S.</p>
        <p>The animal Easter vestry meeting in connection with the above wee held In the vestry on Tuesday evening. The vicar, the Rua. James 1) des, presided, sod there were also present line Rev C Sbirtclitt, Messrs G Armstrong, E Winter, W Milner, C S Daniels and J Hall. Mr. Armstrong submitted the ecotooss which showed a balance in head of £7 130 31. The accounts aere adopted.—The Vicar acid he desired to acknowledge his gratitude to the wardens, sidesmen, the organist and choir, end all the workers in the cht pariah. The fdllowing were elected : Vicar to warden, Mr T U Corbett ; people's warden, 31r T Jolley ; siderunen, Messrs U Armstrong, Id 11 Bretherton. 'l' J Boswell, J Bunch, A Bradshaw, E Bradshaw, J E Goodwin, J 11.11, J llarrison,C A Len, A Owen, G Stringer, I' Taylor, and NV Thomas. lay representatives, Messrs G Armstrong and 11 II Bretherton.—A hearty note,? thanks wee accorded to Mr Armstrong on the proposition of the Vicor; seconded by 31r Winter, for bis services as clerk.</p>
