        <head>GIENTLIRM EN.</head>
        <p>GIENTLIRM EN.</p>
        <p>It afforde me the most rinhounded pleasure to give you particular. as to the result of the use of ' Solaro " on' yself. To begin with, I must by Monroe, and truth- fully state that when I tent for. 1/71d, trial pot of "Salim, " I had no faith in it, end doubtless you will say "no wonder " when I give perticulars of my , ease. Fifteen years ago Eczema paid OA a visit ; a few days sinerswe parted company, hoping and trusting never to meet again, thanks to " Solaro." I have been treated by four doctors for &amp;semi, tall of whom failed to care me. I could name nearly I • hundred of the largely ndvertised preparations, all of which I persevered with, only to find in the end it was purely waste of time, money, ml laboor. Only • nook ago I was atone deaf in my right ear, due to wet Eczema, and as my hearing is of great importance in my trade (cotton), I wait forced to leave my work on hundreds of occasions. The disease commenced io my head in 1800, and for years my heed wee one mem of eruption. You can form some idea as to its condi, ion when I tell you that my hair felt liko a cap glued to my scalp. Brushing or combing the hair wan impotsible. If then attacked my eyes, ears, and chest, and has remained wit h me tip to fire or six days sineo. And now, gentlemen, the disease ha. entirely diaappeared. I can hear •Il right, and there is not even a trace of ECYOIIOI in the whole of any body. And this all ocompliebed with one pot of " Solaro." I obeli alway• consider it my duty to further your interests by informing any sufferers bola kiesemy of the golden virtues of " Solavo." Faithfully yours,</p>
      </div>
