        <p>On the proposition of the Chairman, seconded hy M. Helton, the Council expressed its deep sympathy with Mr. end Mrs. Tnylor in the lone they had eustsined ty the death of their ton.</p>
        <p>Mr. Halton, having expresaed apprecietion of the valuable service. which Mr. Furness had rendered Sr chairman during the past year, saki he way in favour of giving the younger menitieni of the Council. chance of rising to the chair, lie therefore propoted that Mr. Ireland he elected chairman for the ensuing year. Mr. Sherratt seconded and the proposition was unanimously agreed to. . . . . .</p>
