        <p>STOCKTON litoTn 'MAI/ESN snood social in connection with the Stockton Heath Tradesmen's Asenciro ion was held in the Ifel: r ale on Thursday evening. There were cr nsiderehly over ,W ladies and gentlemen preeent and a very enjoyable time was apent. Whist wee indulged in end alter many exciting game. the winners ran but as fdlloore •—Ledies I, Mire Knipht ;2, Mr. Wood ; coneolation, Mr. Wray (playing.. ladv4 I ientlemen I, Mr. Jan heon; 2, Mr. Jowett ; conaniorion, Mr. L. Vern, n. Refreshments wane served and dancing was indulged in until 1 ore. During the evening on behalf of the gentlemen Mr. J. R. Wood (president of the Aesocietion) presented Mr. A. E. Allen II e late secrelery with. gramophone in acknowledgment of his eervices to the association, and on behalf of the ladies Mr.. Weleby handed to him black merhle timepiece. lie evening's orrangi meats were in thelband• of Mr. Houghton secretary of the aesociarion tr in.</p>
