        <p>NEWSAGENT.</p>
        <p>It is with deep rcgret that we announce the death of Mr. Edwy William R. Lowe, newsagent, of .4. hiollrorne-street, and 7, Suez-street. Warringtoo, who maaed an--.y on Thursday at South Grange Villa, Thurmaston, near feint ate, The news ail le teceived with itrotund sort- tw by our readers, for although Mr. 1.01.10 had vever taken pin in public. affairs, he was one of the best known and most highly respected of our townsmen. In Decetriber last, Mr. Lowe had a sudden nervous phystral breakdown and went to etay wi h his n. Mr. E. E. Lowe, curator of the Leicester Municipal Museum and Art Gallery, in hopes of recuperation. Unfortunately bin health contiatred to fail and in spite of every rare and attention he died on Thursday. Mr Loa., was boat at Maccleafield, Cheahire. in 1817 and commenced kin Imaine. career as an ironmonger iu that town. About that be came lo Warrington as manager for Mr. W. S. Pierpviot, then in business as an ironmonger in llorsemarket- sti eet, rear Parr'. Rank. When tits late Mr. Podmore gave np Ilia snit I newspaper shop in 14,160 rue-street in 1890, Mr. Lowe bemire the tenant and, with the aid of Mrs. Lowe, be worked the busineas opt° it {resent position. II s unfit i nag rLee,fnita as and unselfialutese endeared lair to a very large circle of townspeople. lie WM the earl if courteay and no detail Man WO small to tan overlooked if lie thought he rood be of service to oorna. Ilia kindly at nipathy wan another marked characteridic and be. death will Meall to many the Ir t(a true friend. The interment will take place at Thurmistoo, near Leicester, at 3 o'clock to-day (Saturday .</p>
